  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-02T15:29:25.397Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently when you configure full body tracking to freeze trackers upon D/C your lower body gets locked into the position trackers were in the moment they DCd, that makes sense. However if you now rotate your head the entire body spins with it. Thats not how it should be in my opinion. \n\nE.g. when I sleep I will inevitably turn my head even just a little bit, which will result in my avatar getting a broken neck and whatnot.\n\nSo my proposed change is; to lock the rotation of the body relative to the playspace, keeping devices in place while being able to rotate the head. \n\nIf moving the head around would now also move the body (keep offset basically) that'd allow people to use tools like Playspace Mover (OVR AdvancedSettings - Motion) while having tracking frozen.\n\nBut just locking the rotation would already help.\n\nI could also see this becoming a option somewhere in the settings. Maybe by making the toggle for lock tracking into a tristate option:\n\n- not locked\n\n- locked (rotating with head)\n\n- fully locked",
